Pre-change SHA-256:
989cb33b785f542db5993216e18ee84edf3ab803fd93f841c83277e980c3f844  private-receipt-usdc.mjs

The pre-change aggregate verifier always passed `fetchReceiptAs().decoded`
back through `receiptView()`. That value was already normalized, so its public
keys were strings rather than PublicKey objects and `.toBase58()` failed.

To restore the pre-change assertion behavior, replace:

  const view =
    receipt?.receiptIdHex && typeof receipt.authority === "string"
      ? receipt
      : receiptView(receipt);

with:

  const view = receiptView(receipt);
